# Frontend (`apps/web`)

React + TypeScript + Vite + React Router + Zustand + SCSS Modules ([stack](../../docs/tech-stack.md) §2). UI only — conversion runs on the server. Structure — [architecture](../../docs/architecture.md) §3.1. Routes — [task](../../docs/technical-task.md) §4. UI tokens — [design](../../docs/design.md).

## `src/` layout

| Folder | Purpose |
| ------ | ------- |
| `app/` | providers, router, layout |
| `pages/` | route screens (`Home`, `Login`, `Account`, `Share`…) |
| `components/` | reusable UI (Header, Footer, Dropzone, JobStatus…) |
| `features/conversion/` | Zustand: file → upload → poll → result |
| `api/` | thin Nest fetch wrappers |
| `styles/` | tokens / reset |
| `lib/` | чистые утилиты |
| `types/` | доменные типы |
| `constants/` | константы экранов и лимитов |

## Imports / alias `@/`

Алиас `@/` → `src/` (Vite + `tsconfig.app.json`). Oxlint: `import/no-relative-parent-imports` + `no-restricted-imports` по слоям.

- Кросс-папка: `import { Button } from '@/components/Button/Button'`.
- Та же папка и дети маршрута: `./Component.types`, `./Component.module.scss`, `./AccountFileList/AccountFileList`.
- Никогда `../` — вместо этого `@/`.
- `pages` не импортируют другие `pages`. `components` не зависят от `pages` / `features` / `api` / `app`. `features` не зависят от UI. `lib` — только `types` / `constants` / `lib`.

## Rules

- Functional components + `const handleX = ()` for handlers.
- Job/polling state lives in `features/conversion`, not spread across pages.
- Poll job status **every 2s** until `completed` / `failed` ([architecture](../../docs/architecture.md) §4.1).
- Keep conversion business logic out of `api/`; HTTP + error parsing only.
- Styles — **SCSS Modules** next to the component (`Component.module.scss`), not global CSS for everything.
- One component per folder (`tsx` + `module.scss` + `types.ts` if local props exist). Details — [architecture](../../docs/architecture.md) §3.1.
- `import type` from `./Component.types`; do not re-export types from the tsx.
- Conditional UI without an else branch: `{cond && <X />}`, not `{cond ? <X /> : null}`. Keep ternary when both branches render.
- A11y: `aria-label`, keyboard for interactive controls, meaningful `alt` / `role`.
- React Compiler in use — do not add `useMemo`/`useCallback` unless needed.
- Tests: Vitest / Playwright ([stack](../../docs/tech-stack.md) §7).
